  "details": "VRChat has a ton of settings, and I personally changed a lot of them over time. Today, I tried to remember what the default value of many settings was. Trying to remember this is not easy, especially when you have changed a lot of them or when you are a new VRChat user. \n\nOf course, I could uninstall and reinstall VRChat, but I don't think that is a good user experience as this will revert all my settings.\n\nWhat I suggest here is to have a \"revert\" button next to each setting, similar to the FOV setting. So people who like to change settings and new users won't have to worry if they changed something and would like to revert stuff, just click the revert button next to any setting, done!\n\nIt can be individual for each setting or grouped per categories like in the Face Mirror settings, or even hidden like in Blender, where you can revert any value by pressing the Backspace key. Additionally, a \"Revert All\" button somewhere so if a user wants to reset every setting to default, this can be also done globally.",
